T*
() Tj
T*
(Purpose) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Capture the design decision that emerged while comparing the monitoring policies described) Tj
T*
(in the 2004 thesis with the behavior that actually survives in the Perl code, and translate) Tj
T*
(that into a modern persistence model for web-monitor.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Historical observations) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The thesis describes two caching policies. The archive policy stores timestamped snapshots) Tj
T*
(at regular intervals whether or not anything changed; this preserves full history and) Tj
T*
(supports arbitrary historical comparisons, but duplicates unchanged state. The overwrite) Tj
T*
(policy stores a new copy only when content changes; this saves space, but the thesis) Tj
T*
(explicitly notes that history is lost because the previous cached state is overwritten.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The recovered Perl strongly supports the researcher-domain archive path: timestamped) Tj
T*
(snapshots can be written, reloaded, compared, and reported. Only low-level raw-cache helpers) Tj
T*
(survive for the overwrite path; the course-domain comparison logic and conditional-overwrite) Tj
T*
(orchestration are not present in Appendix A.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This matters for the modern port. Recreating only the fully recovered archive behavior would) Tj
T*
(preserve what survived in code, but it would underuse an important design idea that was) Tj
T*
(discussed in the thesis and only partially preserved in the implementation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Decision for web-monitor) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(web-monitor will combine the useful properties of both historical policies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Every scheduled crawl is recorded, but a new full snapshot is persisted only when the) Tj
T*
(observed state differs from the most recent stored state.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(A crawl with no change records that the site was checked at that time and still maps to the) Tj
T*
(existing snapshot. A crawl that finds a change creates a new snapshot and records the) Tj
T*
(transition from the previous state to the new one.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(This avoids storing duplicate full snapshots on every crawl while still preserving) Tj
T*
(historical state.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
